msgid "rules.gendered_roles_label"
msgstr "Gendered Roles"

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_reason"
msgstr ""
"The male generic does not speak to all genders or gender identities. Many "
"people therefore do not feel included in the dialogue."

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_solution"
msgstr ""
"Use words that address the female gender as well as gender identities that "
"do not follow a binary understanding of gender."

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_color"
msgstr "gendered"

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_hierachy_reason"
msgstr ""
"This term communicates an outdated idea of hierarchy and casts the topic of "
"leadership in stereotypical male terms."

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_hierachy_solution"
msgstr ""
"Use terms that assume a supportive notion of leadership and can mean "
"different genders."

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_hierachy_color"
msgstr "gendered"

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_image_reason"
msgstr ""
"This term hides a form that is not gender-neutral and therefore calls up "
"images with masculine connotations in our mind's eye."

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_image_solution"
msgstr "Use alternatives that are gender neutral while avoiding duplication."

msgid "rules.gendered_roles_image_color"
msgstr "gendered"

msgid "rules.gendered_denominations_reason"
msgstr ""
"For economic-historical reasons, an image of a man is unconsciously evoked "
"in front of the inner eye, even if the term is linguistically neutral. The "
"female gender or other gender identities therefore do not become visible. "
"And they will not feel to belong in this setting."

msgid "rules.gendered_denominations_solution"
msgstr ""
"In order to provoke an inclusive image, be not only linguistically, but also"
" mentally neutral in your formulation. Rather use a noun that describes the "
"activity. Or use a denomination that is truly gender-neutral."

msgid "rules.gendered_denominations_color"
msgstr "gendered"

msgid "rules.gendered_language_label"
msgstr "Gendered Language"

msgid "rules.gendered_language_reason"
msgstr ""
"For economic-historical reasons, an image of a man is unconsciously evoked "
"in front of the inner eye, even if the term is linguistically neutral. The "
"female gender or other gender identities do not become visible. And they "
"will not feel to belong in this setting."

msgid "rules.gendered_language_solution"
msgstr ""
"In order to provoke an inclusive image, be not only linguistically, but also"
" mentally neutral in your formulation. Rather use a noun that describes the "
"activity. Or use a denomination that is truly gender-neutral."

msgid "rules.gendered_language_color"
msgstr "gendered"

msgid "rules.agentic_language_label"
msgstr "Agentic Language"

msgid "rules.agentic_language_reason"
msgstr ""
"This term is agentic, describing attributes that enforce the male stereotype"
" as the the norm. People not falling into that stereotype (women but also "
"other underrepresented groups) will feel unconsciously excluded by this "
"word. "

msgid "rules.agentic_language_solution"
msgstr ""
"Use a word combination that sounds more team-oriented and refers to the "
"purpose in work."

msgid "rules.agentic_language_color"
msgstr "non-inclusive"

msgid "rules.communal_language_label"
msgstr "Communal Language"

msgid "rules.communal_language_reason"
msgstr ""
"This term uses communal language and emphasizes cooperative characteristics "
"and thus inclusive attributes. People from diverse backgrounds will be "
"unconsciously attracted by this word."

msgid "rules.communal_language_solution"
msgstr ""
"Use more of such words or formulations expressing cooperation, care or "
"purpose."

msgid "rules.communal_language_color"
msgstr "inclusive"

msgid "rules.d_and_i_words_label"
msgstr "Inclusive Words"

msgid "rules.d_and_i_words_reason"
msgstr ""
"This term describes that the company values diversity and/or inclusion. Such"
" a public commitment is appreciated by underrepresented groups."

msgid "rules.d_and_i_words_solution"
msgstr ""
"Make it clear through your words, if possible, that diversity is desired in "
"your company and that you are working towards an inclusive culture."

msgid "rules.d_and_i_words_color"
msgstr "inclusive"

msgid "rules.empty_words_label"
msgstr "Empty Words"

msgid "rules.empty_words_reason"
msgstr ""
"This is a term that has become a hollow word because it has been overused in"
" the business environment."

msgid "rules.empty_words_solution"
msgstr ""
"Avoid using this word. Instead, explain the situation in a tangible and "
"descriptive way."

msgid "rules.empty_words_color"
msgstr "style"

msgid "rules.salary_vague_or_misleading_reason"
msgstr "Missing"

msgid "rules.salary_vague_or_misleading_solution"
msgstr "Missing"

msgid "rules.salary_vague_or_misleading_color"
msgstr "style"

msgid "rules.verbose_reason"
msgstr "Missing"

msgid "rules.verbose_solution"
msgstr "Missing"

msgid "rules.verbose_color"
msgstr "style"

msgid "rules.vague_ambiguous_reason"
msgstr "Missing"

msgid "rules.vague_ambiguous_solution"
msgstr "Missing"

msgid "rules.vague_ambiguous_color"
msgstr "style"

msgid "rules.boasting_words_label"
msgstr "Boasting Words"

msgid "rules.boasting_words_reason"
msgstr ""
"With this term you use a language of superlatives. Many people perceive this"
" as negative, as it gives the impression of having to conform in terms of "
"superlatives."

msgid "rules.boasting_words_solution"
msgstr "Use an authentic and honest sounding statement."

msgid "rules.boasting_words_color"
msgstr "style"

msgid "rules.gendered_pronouns_label"
msgstr "Gendered Pronouns"

msgid "rules.gendered_pronouns_reason"
msgstr ""
"According to linguistic specifications, masculine pronouns mean all persons."
" However, behavioural economics shows that this does not work. Women or non-"
"binary people do not feel addressed by the \"male generic\" and their "
"engagement decreases."

msgid "rules.gendered_pronouns_solution"
msgstr ""
"If possible, use the direct form of address (you). This makes the text more "
"emotional and eliminates the wrong gender trigger. If you have to write in "
"the third person, use \"they\". "

msgid "rules.gendered_pronouns_color"
msgstr "gendered"

msgid "rules.stereotypes_label"
msgstr "Stereotypes"

msgid "rules.stereotypes_reason"
msgstr ""
"This expression uses an outdated and perhaps even discriminatory stereotype "
"that pigeonholes members of the social group concerned and hinders them to "
"use their full potential. "

msgid "rules.stereotypes_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself a \"flip it\" question, e.g. \"Would I write the same if this "
"person was white / young / male / rich, etc.?\" This will trigger a mental "
"process that will bring you to a better wording."

msgid "rules.stereotypes_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.gendered_stereotypes_label"
msgstr "Gendered Stereotypes"

msgid "rules.gendered_stereotypes_reason"
msgstr ""
"The exclusive use of the feminine form in relation to certain activities "
"traps women in outdated stereotypes and prevents them from developing their "
"full potential. This is discriminatory against women AND men and non-binary "
"people."

msgid "rules.gendered_stereotypes_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself a \"flip it\" question, e.g. \"Would I write the same if this "
"person was male?\" This triggers a mental process that brining you to a "
"better wording."

msgid "rules.gendered_stereotypes_color"
msgstr "gendered"

msgid "rules.biased_language_label"
msgstr "Biased Language"

msgid "rules.biased_language_reason"
msgstr ""
"This expression uses an outdated and perhaps even discriminatory stereotype "
"that pigeonholes members of the social group concerned and hinders them to "
"use their full potential. "

msgid "rules.biased_language_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself a \"flip it\" question, e.g. \"Would I write the same if this "
"person was white / young / male / rich, etc.?\" This triggers a mental "
"process bringing you to a better wording."

msgid "rules.biased_language_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.ability_bias_reason"
msgstr ""
"This expression uses an outdated and perhaps even discriminatory stereotype "
"that pigeonholes people with disabilities (physical or mental) and hinders "
"them to use their full potential. "

msgid "rules.ability_bias_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself the \"flip it\" question \"Would I write the same if this "
"person had no disabilities?\" This triggers a mental process bringing you to"
" a better wording."

msgid "rules.ability_bias_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.age_bias_old_reason"
msgstr ""
"This expression uses an outdated and perhaps even discriminatory stereotype "
"that pigeonholes people aged 50 and over and hinders them to use their full "
"potential. "

msgid "rules.age_bias_old_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself the \"flip it\" question \"Would I write the same thing if this"
" person was 35 years old?\" This triggers a mental process that helps you to"
" formulate better."

msgid "rules.age_bias_old_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.age_bias_young_reason"
msgstr ""
"This expression uses an outdated and perhaps even discriminatory stereotype "
"that pigeonholes people aged 25 and below and hinders them to use their full"
" potential. "

msgid "rules.age_bias_young_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself the \"flip it\" question \"Would I write the same thing if this"
" person was 35 years old?\" This triggers a mental process that helps you to"
" formulate better."

msgid "rules.age_bias_young_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.culture_bias_reason"
msgstr ""
"This expression uses an outdated and perhaps even discriminatory stereotype "
"that pigeonholes people of a different culture and and hinders them to use "
"their full potential. "

msgid "rules.culture_bias_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself the \"flip it\" question \"Would I write the same thing if this"
" person had the same nationality/culture as I?\" This triggers a mental "
"process that helps you to formulate better."

msgid "rules.culture_bias_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.migration_background_bias_reason"
msgstr ""
"This expression can be difficult to understand for people with a migration "
"background, as they may not understand certain idioms or bureaucratic "
"language."

msgid "rules.migration_background_bias_solution"
msgstr ""
"Rephrase the expression with a simpler choice of words. This makes the text "
"more easily readable."

msgid "rules.migration_background_bias_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.anti_lgtbqiplus_bias_reason"
msgstr ""
"This term describes an outdated and perhaps even discriminatory "
"understanding of gender or sexual orientation that pigeonholes LGBTQIA+ "
"people and hinders their fulfilment."

msgid "rules.anti_lgtbqiplus_bias_solution"
msgstr ""
"Ask yourself the \"flip it\" question \"Would I write the same thing if this"
" person were either male/female or heterosexual?\" This triggers a mental "
"process that helps you to formulate better."

msgid "rules.anti_lgtbqiplus_bias_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.classism_bias_reason"
msgstr ""
"Due to their education or economic possibilities, this expression can seem "
"arrogant or incomprehensible to people as they associate this word "
"combination with the higher social classes."

msgid "rules.classism_bias_solution"
msgstr ""
"Rephrase the expression to make it less complex. This makes the text more "
"easily readable."

msgid "rules.classism_bias_color"
msgstr "discriminating"

msgid "rules.old_language_reason"
msgstr ""
"This combination of words may no longer be familiar to young people, as "
"language is always evolving."

msgid "rules.old_language_solution"
msgstr ""
"Reflect on whether this expression is still in use outside your age group. "
"If not, try to formulate its meaning differently."

msgid "rules.old_language_color"
msgstr "style"

msgid "rules.new_language_reason"
msgstr ""
"This combination of words may not be comprehensible to older generations, as"
" language is always being created anew, especially among younger "
"generations."

msgid "rules.new_language_solution"
msgstr ""
"Reflect on whether this expression is still in use outside your age group. "
"If not, try to formulate its meaning differently."

msgid "rules.new_language_color"
msgstr "style"

